<!--
  ============================================================================
  BodySizeIsReal.xml                        Jawa_Patches - new file 2026-08-22
  ============================================================================

  OWNER, 2026-08-22: "It would be very appropriate for Wookiee to TOWER over Jawa
  and even humans, by the lore. That's pretty important actually. And the same the
  other way for smallness. size differential makes great immersion as well as nice
  mechanics differentials during unfortunate times like melee."

  🔴 EVERY SIZE GENE THE STAR WARS PACK SHIPS IS COSMETIC. Verified in our own
  source: `RimMandrake_BodySizeGene_big/bigger/biggest/small/smaller` all write
  `SM_Cosmetic_BodySizeOffset`, and a repo-wide grep finds 10 uses of that stat and
  ZERO of `SM_BodySizeOffset`. ⇒ a Wookiee and a Jawa have had IDENTICAL mechanical
  body size all along: same health scale, same melee damage, same carry capacity,
  same food. The pictures differed and nothing else did.

  Big and Small ships the real ladder. Baseline human BodySize is 1.0:

      BS_RabbitFrame / GnomeFrame   -0.60  ->  0.40
      BS_SmallFrame  / DwarfFrame   -0.35  ->  0.65     <- used here
      (nothing between -0.35 and 0)
      BS_LargeFrame                 +0.40  ->  1.40     <- used here
      HalfColossusFrame             +0.70  ->  1.70
      HalfJotunFrame                +0.75  ->  1.75
      OgreFrame                     +1.00  ->  2.00     ⚠️ see below
      JotunFrame                    +1.50  ->  2.50
      GreatOgreFrame                +2.00  ->  3.00
      TitanFrame                    +3.00  ->  4.00

  ⇒ A Wookiee at 1.40 against a Jawa at 0.65 is a **2.15x** differential, in health
  scale and melee and carry capacity, not just in the sprite.

  🔑 WHY THESE ARE SWAPS AND NOT ADDITIONS. Our cosmetic genes and Big and Small's
  real frames share the SAME `exclusionTags` entry, `BodySize`. Two active genes
  with a shared exclusion tag fight in `Pawn_GeneTracker.CheckForOverrides` and one
  silently wins - which one is not worth relying on. So the cosmetic gene is
  REPLACED, never stacked. Where a species had no size gene at all the operation is
  an Add instead, and both cases are marked below.

  ⚠️ ONE RUNG FOR EVERYONE LARGE, DELIBERATELY. Feeorin and Lasat carried the +0.50
  cosmetic rung and Wookiee the +0.20, and all of them land on `BS_LargeFrame`.
  A first pass that is consistent is easier to tune than one that is already
  opinionated: promoting a single species to `HalfJotunFrame` later is a one-line
  edit, and nothing here has to be undone first.

  ⛔ NOBODY IS GIVEN `OgreFrame` OR ABOVE, AND THAT IS A DECISION. At +1.00 Big and
  Small grants the `BS_Giant` trait automatically, which is the permission flag for
  the 23 `BS_GiantWeapon` weapons. Putting a species on that rung silently hands it
  giant weapons as well as size. Those are two separate questions and this file
  answers only the first.

  ⛔ TALL IS NOT BIG, and the two tools exist for the two meanings. Species that are
  tall but slender KEEP their cosmetic gene and are deliberately absent from this
  file: Kaminoan (2.7 m, the tallest on the roster, and canonically frail), Muun
  (1.9 m gaunt), Cerean, Kel Dor, Gungan, Ithorian, Chagrian, Aqualish, Nagai, Pyke.
  Giving them real mass would make a frail cloner a melee threat.

  ⚠️ NOT INCLUDED, EACH FOR A NAMED REASON:
    * `RimMandrakeRakata` - 2.0 m but only ~85 kg, and its own def uses a gaunt body.
      Human mass; the height is cosmetic work, not this.
    * `RimMandrakeNelvaanian` - males 2.0 m / 130 kg, females 1.5 m / 50 kg. A gene
      applies to the whole xenotype and would make the females giants too.
    * `RimMandrakeHutt` - carries the +0.70 cosmetic rung and is genuinely enormous,
      but a Hutt is sluglike and does not fight hand to hand. Real mass would make it
      tanky in melee, which may be exactly right or exactly wrong. OWNER'S CALL.
    * `RimMandrakeYoderForceGremlin` IS included at `BS_SmallFrame` (0.65), but the
      species is ~0.66 m in lore, which argues for `BS_RabbitFrame` (0.40). One rung
      lower is a one-line change if wanted.

  ⚠️ METABOLISM MOVES WITH SIZE and that is the mechanic, not a side effect.
  `BS_LargeFrame` is met -2 (a big body eats more) and `BS_SmallFrame` is met +5.
  On a xenotype this is a permanent property of the species.
  ============================================================================
-->
<Patch>

  <!-- ═══ LARGE: swapping the cosmetic Big Frame for a real one ═══════════ -->

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>Defs/XenotypeDef[defName="RimMandrakeWookiee"]/genes/li[text()="RimMandrake_BodySizeGene_big"]</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationReplace">
      <xpath>Defs/XenotypeDef[defName="RimMandrakeWookiee"]/genes/li[text()="RimMandrake_BodySizeGene_big"]</xpath>
      <value><li MayRequire="redmattis.bigsmall.core">BS_LargeFrame</li></value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>Defs/XenotypeDef[defName="RimMandrakeSithMassassi"]/genes/li[text()="RimMandrake_BodySizeGene_big"]</xpath>
